{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ויהי בנסוע", :translit "vayehi binsoa", :gloss "and it was when it set forward"} {:he "ויהי עולה", :translit "vayehi oleh", :gloss "'and it was' rises to"} {:he "ל\"א", :translit "lamed alef", :gloss "31"} {:he "ל\"א מלכים", :translit "lamed alef melakhim", :gloss "31 kings"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "ויהי", :b "ל\"א"}], :frame {:text "Joshua waged war against 31 kings on the west side of the Jordan (Joshua 12:24 counts them). The inverted and detached nunim that frame Numbers 10:35-36 are treated as a separate book of Torah by the Sages (Shabbat 115b-116a). The Ba'al HaTurim links the numerical value of ויהי to these 31 kings, suggesting that the ark's journeying signifies divine warfare against them.", :sources ["Joshua 12:24" "Shabbat 115b-116a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "בנסע", :translit "binsoa", :gloss "when it set forward"} {:he "קומה ה'", :translit "kumah Hashem", :gloss "Rise up, YHWH"} {:he "בנסע הארון", :translit "binsoa ha-aron", :gloss "when the ark set forward"} {:he "המרכבה וחיות הקדש", :translit "ha-merkhavah ve-khiyot ha-kodesh", :gloss "the Chariot and the holy beasts"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Midrashic reading: the ark physically swayed before departing, waiting for Moses' proclamation"}], :frame {:text "Ezekiel 1 describes the divine Chariot (merkavah) and its holy beasts (chayot ha-kodesh) that bear the divine presence. The Targum Yonatan to Numbers 10:35 renders 'when the ark set forward' as an allusion to the divine Chariot being set in motion, indicating that the earthly ark and the supernal Chariot move in concert.", :sources ["Ezekiel 1" "Targum Yonatan Numbers 10:35"]}} {:quotes [{:he "בנסע", :translit "binsoa", :gloss "when it set forward"} {:he "חשמ\"ל", :translit "chashmal", :gloss "chashmal (amber/electrum)"} {:he "שטח\"ז", :translit "shetachaz", :gloss "shin-tav-chet-zayin"} {:he "ככבוד המרכבה", :translit "ke-khvod ha-merkhavah", :gloss "like the glory of the Chariot"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Atbash of בנסע yields שטחז, then further exchanged via alef-bet/bet-shin to produce חשמ\"ל"} {:kind :gematria, :a "שטח\"ז", :b "ככבוד המרכבה"}], :frame {:text "Ezekiel 1:4 describes the vision of the divine Chariot in which חשמל (chashmal) appears as part of the theophanic spectacle. The Ba'al HaTurim links the ark's journey to the merkavah by showing that בנסע, through atbash and letter-exchange, transforms into חשמל, the radiant substance of the divine Chariot.", :sources ["Ezekiel 1:4"]}} {:quotes [{:he "בנסע", :translit "binsoa", :gloss "when it set forward"} {:he "יעקב", :translit "yaakov", :gloss "Jacob"} {:he "דמות יעקב", :translit "demut yaakov", :gloss "likeness of Jacob"} {:he "חקוק בכסא הכבוד", :translit "chakuk bi-khise ha-kavod", :gloss "engraved on the Throne of Glory"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "בנסע", :b "יעקב"}], :frame {:text "The Midrash states that the likeness of Jacob is engraved upon the Throne of Glory (Genesis Rabbah 68:12, also cited in connection with the divine chariot imagery in Pirkei de-Rabbi Eliezer 3). By equating the gematria of בנסע with יעקב, the Ba'al HaTurim suggests that the ark's journeying carries with it the patriarch's engraved image on the supernal throne.", :sources ["Bereshit Rabbah 68:12" "Pirkei de-Rabbi Eliezer 3"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "ויהי", :a-value 31, :b "ל\"א", :b-value 31, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true} {:kind :other, :note "Midrashic reading: the ark physically swayed before departing, waiting for Moses' proclamation", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Atbash of בנסע yields שטחז, then further exchanged via alef-bet/bet-shin to produce חשמ\"ל", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "שטח\"ז", :a-value 324, :b "ככבוד המרכבה", :b-value 324, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true} {:kind :gematria, :a "בנסע", :a-value 182, :b "יעקב", :b-value 182, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:28:22.196730170Z", :model "glm-5.2"}